# Copy to .env (gitignored). All keys are optional.
#
# --- Multi-instance identity (only needed for bare `docker compose up`) -------
# The Makefile derives these from your git branch automatically, so `make up`
# needs nothing here. Set them only if you run `docker compose up` directly and
# want a non-default instance name / hostname (e.g. to run two checkouts at
# once). Compose reads .env for ${VAR} substitution in compose.yml.
#   COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=scoria-myfeature
#   SCORIA_HOST=scoria-myfeature.localhost
#
# --- LLM critique pass -------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for the screenshot critique pass; the screenshot-only pass needs
# no key.
#   docker compose --profile shots run --rm critique
#   # or natively:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a; mix scoria.ui.shots --critique
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
